//@version=6
// prior-4h-lines v2026.11.22.25 — version is in the indicator title too: if the chart legend
// v2026.11.22.23: the v.22 event-log arrow redraw was reverted at Victor's call — in live use it dropped the line tags and never cleared past-frame arrows. This build is the v.21 behaviour (tags + flip-time arrows), version bumped.
// v2026.11.22.24: line tags one font size smaller (size.tiny) — frame, STOP and RANGE tags; arrows unchanged.
// v2026.11.22.25: indicator renamed to 4h-signals-only at Victor's ask; the version stays in the title so the legend check still works.
// does not show this exact version, the chart is running an older copy.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// PRIOR 4H LINES — the rolling prior-candle frame: the HIGH, LOW and OPEN of
// the LAST COMPLETED 4H candle, drawn from that candle's open, through it and
// through the candle now forming. When a 4H candle closes, the lines move to
// it — it becomes the prior — and so on, candle after candle. The new candle
// is traded against the prior candle, nothing else.
//
//   • HIGH line (red), tag "HIGH <price>" — the prior candle's top.
//   • LOW line (green), tag "LOW <price>" — the prior candle's bottom.
//   • OPEN line (gray), tag "OPEN <price>" — where the prior candle started;
//     its reclaim or loss is judged on 10-minute closes.
//   • CLOSE line (dark gray), tag "CLOSE <price>" — where the prior candle
//     settled. A visual reference only (price stalling above or below it
//     is the read); it is not an entry line (added v2026.11.22.8).
//   • The tags name the LINE, never a direction: there is no trade until
//     price interacts — a break or a reclaim at the line decides, and the
//     same line can produce either side (v2026.11.22.5 dropped the old
//     permanent SHORT / LONG tags for exactly that reason).
//   • CONFLUENCE: when a line sits within 0.1% of the prior day's high or
//     low (PDH / PDL) or the prior week's high or low (PWH / PWL), the tag
//     says so — "HIGH 1728.46 + PWH" — the same callout the signal cards
//     make. Toggle in the settings.
//   • MERGED LINES: when the candle's own values coincide within 0.1% —
//     the open at the high, the open at the low — only ONE line is drawn,
//     tagged with both names: "HIGH + OPEN 1728.46". No stacked lines,
//     no double tags (v2026.11.22.6). Lines are drawn only when needed.
//   • RANGE lines (dashed by default), tags "RANGE HIGH <price>" /
//     "RANGE LOW <price>" — the MOTHER candle: an older completed 4H
//     candle whose high and low were never broken, with every candle
//     since built inside her range. Her edges are context for the
//     range trade later; they stay drawn until a completed candle
//     closes outside her (added v2026.11.22.20). Toggle in settings.
//   • CROSSING ARROWS (v2026.11.22.16; losses added v2026.11.22.19;
//     step engine fixed v2026.11.22.21 — the security-fetched 10m bar
//     time never arrived, so the machines never stepped; they now
//     step on the completed bar's own close / low / high changing):
//     every completed 10-minute close that crosses a level gets a
//     small arrow in the level's colour on that 10m bar — under it
//     pointing up for a close crossing upward, above it pointing
//     down for a close crossing downward. Crossings alternate by
//     construction: the first is the LOSS (the level taken), the
//     next is the RECLAIM, then a fresh loss, and so on — so a level
//     price chops across shows its flip-flops as alternating arrows.
//     Applies to HIGH, LOW and CLOSE. Arrows belong to the current
//     candle's frame and clear when the frame rolls.
//   • STOP LINES (faint yellow, dashed by default — restyle in
//     settings; the STOP tag sits at the END of the line, with the
//     other tags):
//     when a trade is live — a manipulation sweep back inside, or a
//     break holding beyond a level — the STOP is the FORMING candle's
//     far extreme: its HIGH for a short-side trade (sweep of the prior
//     high, or break of the prior low), its LOW for a long-side trade
//     (sweep of the prior low, or break of the prior high). The stop
//     is NEVER the entry level itself — a stop at the entry is a
//     zero-risk non-trade (Victor, 2026-11-22; the v.11 break stop sat
//     on the broken level and was replaced). If the candle's far
//     extreme is not beyond the entry (a gap-and-go that never came
//     back), no stop is drawn — the candle offered no risk point.
//     If the stop lands on a frame line (within 0.1% — e.g. a sweep
//     that barely crossed the prior high), they MERGE like the frame
//     lines do: one line, the tag gains STOP — "HIGH + STOP 1728.46".
//     Once a stop is TAKEN OUT — a completed 10m close beyond it —
//     the line is removed for the rest of the candle: the trade is
//     invalidated (v2026.11.22.17). A merged tag reverts to the plain
//     frame tag at the same moment. Until it is taken out the stop
//     line STAYS — locked at the extreme that created it, never
//     removed just because the trade case flips or fades
//     (v2026.11.22.18); only the frame roll clears it otherwise.
//   • Tags carry the price, so the level can be checked at a glance.
//   • The 4H values are the chart's own 4H series (extended hours included —
//     the 24h grid), read settled [1] so the lines never repaint mid-candle.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
indicator("4h-signals-only · v2026.11.22.28", shorttitle = "4h-signals-only", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

extend_h = input.int(4, "Extend lines past the candle close (hours)", minval = 0, maxval = 24, tooltip = "How far the lines reach past the current 4H candle's close, so the tags stay readable.")
showConf = input.bool(true, "Tag confluence with PDH / PDL / PWH / PWL", tooltip = "When a prior-4H line sits within 0.1% of the prior day's or prior week's high/low, the tag names it.")

// Every line can be hidden, restyled (solid / dashed / dotted) and
// re-weighted (width 1–10) in the settings — checkbox, style and
// width sit on one row per line. A merged line takes the settings of
// its highest-priority VISIBLE member and is tagged with the visible
// names only; hide every member and the line is not drawn at all.
gL = "Lines — show / hide · style · width"
showHigh   = input.bool(true,  "HIGH",  inline = "lh", group = gL)
styleHigh  = input.string("solid",  "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "lh", group = gL)
widthHigh  = input.int(2, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "lh", group = gL)
showLow    = input.bool(true,  "LOW",   inline = "ll", group = gL)
styleLow   = input.string("solid",  "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "ll", group = gL)
widthLow   = input.int(2, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "ll", group = gL)
showOpen   = input.bool(true,  "OPEN",  inline = "lo", group = gL)
styleOpen  = input.string("solid",  "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "lo", group = gL)
widthOpen  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "lo", group = gL)
showClose  = input.bool(true,  "CLOSE", inline = "lc", group = gL)
styleClose = input.string("solid",  "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "lc", group = gL)
widthClose = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "lc", group = gL)
showRange  = input.bool(true,  "RANGE (unbroken 4H)", inline = "lr", group = gL, tooltip = "The mother candle: an older completed 4H candle whose HIGH and LOW were never broken, with every candle since built inside her. Her edges stay drawn as context until a completed candle closes outside her.")
styleRange = input.string("dashed", "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "lr", group = gL)
widthRange = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "lr", group = gL)
showStop   = input.bool(true,  "STOP (manipulation wick)", inline = "ls", group = gL, tooltip = "Auto STOP line at the forming candle's far extreme while a trade is live: its high for a short-side trade, its low for a long-side trade. Never the entry level itself.")
styleStop  = input.string("dashed", "", options = ["solid", "dashed", "dotted"], inline = "ls", group = gL)
widthStop  = input.int(1, "", minval = 1, maxval = 10, inline = "ls", group = gL)
showRec    = input.bool(true, "Arrows: lost → reclaim (10m close)", group = gL, tooltip = "Small arrow on every 10m close that crosses a HIGH, LOW or CLOSE level — the loss and the reclaim alike. Follows each level's own show / hide above.")

// ── Signal alerts (prior-4H HIGH & LOW only) ──────────────────────
// Fire a webhook-ready alert on every 10m close that crosses the prior 4H
// HIGH or LOW. Break (go-with) and sweep-reclaim / reject (fade) are both
// emitted, judged on the CLOSE (so a gap-through still fires), and a level
// re-arms the instant it crosses back — the crossing machine alternates by
// design. Bind ONE alert per symbol on this indicator with "Any alert() call"
// and point the webhook at /tv/webhook. Prior-4H high/low only — OPEN / CLOSE
// / RANGE lines are drawing context, never signals.
gA = "Signal alerts (webhook)"
alertsOn = input.bool(true, "Send break / fade alerts (prior-4H + RANGE high & low)", group = gA, tooltip = "ON = emit an alert() on each 10m close that breaks or reclaims/rejects the prior 4H high/low AND the RANGE high/low (mother candle) — all through the SAME break/reclaim logic. Break of a low → SHORT (stop = forming high); reclaim of a low → LONG (stop = forming low); break of a high → LONG (stop = forming low); reject of a high → SHORT (stop = forming high). RANGE alerts need the RANGE toggle on.")

c_high  = #FF0000
c_low   = #43A047
c_open  = #787B86
c_close = #424242
c_stop  = color.new(#FFEB3B, 35)
confPct = 0.1  // shared tolerance %: confluence tags + merging the candle's own lines
f_txtcol(color c) => (color.r(c) * 0.299 + color.g(c) * 0.587 + color.b(c) * 0.114) > 150 ? color.black : color.white
f_lstyle(string s) => s == "dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

// One step of a level's crossing state machine, fed with completed
// 10m closes. Returns [new side, new lost flag, reclaimed?, crossed?]:
// the first close across the level is the LOSS, the next close back
// across it is the RECLAIM, then the cycle restarts. Every crossing
// (loss or reclaim) earns an arrow.
f_flip(int side, bool lost, float price, float level) =>
    int ns = price > level ? 1 : price < level ? -1 : side
    bool flip = side != 0 and ns != 0 and ns != side
    bool rec = flip and lost
    bool nlost = flip ? not lost : lost
    [ns, nlost, rec, flip]

// Build a /tv/webhook-ready JSON payload for one signal. Prices are strings
// (the adapter casts them); symbol + exchange are split so normalize_symbol
// can strip the prefix. Targets are omitted — the webhook computes them from
// entry + stop + direction.
f_sigJSON(string ruleName, string dir, float entryP, float stopP) =>
    '{"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","exchange":"' + syminfo.prefix + '","price":"' + str.tostring(entryP, format.mintick) + '","rule":"' + ruleName + '","direction":"' + dir + '","interval":"10","entry":"' + str.tostring(entryP, format.mintick) + '","stop":"' + str.tostring(stopP, format.mintick) + '"}'

// Prior completed 4H candle's HIGH/LOW/OPEN and its open time, plus the
// forming candle's close time — settled [1] + lookahead, the same idiom as
// 4h-prior-rails and day-signals.
tid = syminfo.tickerid
[pH, pL, pO, pC, tPriorOpen, tClose] = request.security(tid, "240", [high[1], low[1], open[1], close[1], time[1], time_close], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// The FORMING 4H candle's live values (for the manipulation-wick STOP
// line) — read unshifted with lookahead_on; only used on the last bar.
[fH, fL, fC, tFormOpen] = request.security(tid, "240", [high, low, close, time], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// The last COMPLETED 10-minute bar (for the lost → reclaim arrows) —
// judged on 10m closes on any chart timeframe. No bar time is
// fetched with it: in live testing the security-fetched time[1]
// came back na and silently stopped the arrow machines from ever
// stepping (v2026.11.22.21) — the machines step on the bar's own
// close / low / high changing instead, and arrows are stamped with
// the chart's own previous-bar time.
[c10, l10, h10] = request.security(tid, "10", [close[1], low[1], high[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// Older completed 4H candles (offsets 2–9) for the RANGE walk below.
[h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9] = request.security(tid, "240", [high[2], high[3], high[4], high[5], high[6], high[7], high[8], high[9]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[l2, l3, l4, l5, l6, l7, l8, l9] = request.security(tid, "240", [low[2], low[3], low[4], low[5], low[6], low[7], low[8], low[9]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[t2, t3, t4, t5, t6, t7, t8, t9] = request.security(tid, "240", [time[2], time[3], time[4], time[5], time[6], time[7], time[8], time[9]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ── RANGE — the unbroken mother candle ────────────────────────────
// Walk back from the prior candle: an older candle that fully
// contains every candle after it is the mother — her HIGH and LOW
// were never broken and the candles since built inside her. Her
// edges are the context range until a completed candle closes
// outside her (then the walk finds no mother and nothing draws).
float rngHi = na
float rngLo = na
int rngT = na
if showRange and not na(pH) and not na(pL)
    float[] cH = array.from(pH, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, h7, h8, h9)
    float[] cL = array.from(pL, l2, l3, l4, l5, l6, l7, l8, l9)
    int[]   cT = array.from(tPriorOpen, t2, t3, t4, t5, t6, t7, t8, t9)
    float accHi = pH
    float accLo = pL
    int mother = 0
    for i = 1 to 8
        float hiI = array.get(cH, i)
        float loI = array.get(cL, i)
        if na(hiI) or na(loI)
            break
        if hiI >= accHi and loI <= accLo
            mother := i
            accHi := hiI
            accLo := loI
        else
            break
    if mother >= 1
        rngHi := accHi
        rngLo := accLo
        rngT := array.get(cT, mother)

// Confluence levels — prior completed day / week high & low, same settled
// [1] + lookahead idiom.
pdh = request.security(tid, "D", high[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pdl = request.security(tid, "D", low[1],  lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pwh = request.security(tid, "W", high[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
pwl = request.security(tid, "W", low[1],  lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// " + PDH + PWL" style suffix for a price sitting within 0.1% of a
// confluence level; empty when nothing stacks.
f_conf(float price) =>
    string s = ""
    if showConf
        if not na(pdh) and math.abs(price - pdh) / price * 100 <= confPct
            s += " + PDH"
        if not na(pdl) and math.abs(price - pdl) / price * 100 <= confPct
            s += " + PDL"
        if not na(pwh) and math.abs(price - pwh) / price * 100 <= confPct
            s += " + PWH"
        if not na(pwl) and math.abs(price - pwl) / price * 100 <= confPct
            s += " + PWL"
    s

// ── draw — rebuilt on the last bar (delete-then-redraw, the house pattern) ──
var line[]  _ln = array.new_line()
var label[] _lb = array.new_label()
// Locked STOP prices for the forming candle + taken-out flags. A
// stop locks at the far extreme the moment its trade case goes live
// and then does not move; a completed 10m close beyond the lock
// takes it out, and nothing else removes it before the frame rolls.
var float stopSP = na
var bool  stopSDead = false
var float stopLP = na
var bool  stopLDead = false
if barstate.islast and not na(pH) and not na(pL) and not na(pO) and not na(pC) and not na(tPriorOpen) and not na(tClose)
    if array.size(_ln) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(_ln) - 1
            line.delete(array.get(_ln, i))
        array.clear(_ln)
    if array.size(_lb) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(_lb) - 1
            label.delete(array.get(_lb, i))
        array.clear(_lb)
    int tEnd = tClose + extend_h * 3600 * 1000
    // Draw HIGH / LOW / OPEN / CLOSE, merging any whose values
    // coincide (within confPct of the group's first price) into ONE
    // line tagged with every name it carries, in HIGH, LOW, OPEN,
    // CLOSE order. The merged line sits at its highest-priority
    // member (HIGH first, CLOSE last) and takes its colour / width.
    // Lines are drawn only when needed — no stacked duplicates.
    string[] nm = array.from("HIGH", "LOW", "OPEN", "CLOSE")
    float[]  pr = array.from(pH, pL, pO, pC)
    color[]  cl = array.from(c_high, c_low, c_open, c_close)
    int[]    wd = array.from(widthHigh, widthLow, widthOpen, widthClose)
    bool[]   en = array.from(showHigh, showLow, showOpen, showClose)
    string[] sy = array.from(styleHigh, styleLow, styleOpen, styleClose)
    int[]    ix = array.from(0, 1, 2, 3)
    for i = 0 to 2
        for j = 0 to 2 - i
            if array.get(pr, array.get(ix, j)) > array.get(pr, array.get(ix, j + 1))
                int tmp = array.get(ix, j)
                array.set(ix, j, array.get(ix, j + 1))
                array.set(ix, j + 1, tmp)
    int g = 0
    // drawn groups, remembered so a STOP landing on one can merge
    // into its tag instead of drawing a second line
    string[] grpNamesArr = array.new_string()
    float[]  grpPriceArr = array.new_float()
    string[] grpConfArr  = array.new_string()
    label[]  grpLabelArr = array.new_label()
    while g < 4
        int firstIx = array.get(ix, g)
        float gPrice = array.get(pr, firstIx)
        int[] members = array.new_int()
        array.push(members, firstIx)
        int h = g + 1
        while h < 4 and math.abs(array.get(pr, array.get(ix, h)) - gPrice) / gPrice * 100 <= confPct
            array.push(members, array.get(ix, h))
            h += 1
        // visible members only — a merged line answers to the
        // highest-priority member that is switched on
        int[] emembers = array.new_int()
        for m = 0 to array.size(members) - 1
            if array.get(en, array.get(members, m))
                array.push(emembers, array.get(members, m))
        if array.size(emembers) > 0
            int rep = array.get(emembers, 0)
            bool hasH = false
            bool hasL = false
            for m = 0 to array.size(emembers) - 1
                int mi = array.get(emembers, m)
                if mi < rep
                    rep := mi
                if mi == 0
                    hasH := true
                if mi == 1
                    hasL := true
            string tag = ""
            for p = 0 to 3
                bool inp = false
                for m = 0 to array.size(emembers) - 1
                    if array.get(emembers, m) == p
                        inp := true
                if inp
                    tag += (tag == "" ? "" : " + ") + array.get(nm, p)
            float repPrice = array.get(pr, rep)
            string tagNames = tag
            string confStr = f_conf(repPrice)
            tag += " " + str.tostring(repPrice, format.mintick) + confStr
            string st = hasH ? label.style_label_up : hasL ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_left
            array.push(_ln, line.new(tPriorOpen, repPrice, tEnd, repPrice, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = array.get(cl, rep), width = array.get(wd, rep), style = f_lstyle(array.get(sy, rep))))
            array.push(_lb, label.new(tEnd, repPrice, tag, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = st, color = array.get(cl, rep), textcolor = f_txtcol(array.get(cl, rep)), size = size.tiny))
            array.push(grpNamesArr, tagNames)
            array.push(grpPriceArr, repPrice)
            array.push(grpConfArr, confStr)
            array.push(grpLabelArr, array.get(_lb, array.size(_lb) - 1))
        g := h
    // STOP lines — the forming candle's far extreme, never the entry
    // level itself (a stop at the entry is a zero-risk non-trade):
    // short side live = sweep of the high back inside, or break of
    // the low → STOP at the forming candle's HIGH (the wick above).
    // Long side live = sweep of the low back inside, or break of the
    // high → STOP at the forming candle's LOW. The extreme must sit
    // beyond the entry, else the candle offered no risk point and
    // nothing is drawn.
    if showStop and not na(fH) and not na(fL) and not na(fC)
        // A stop is born when its trade case goes live, locks at the
        // candle's far extreme, and then STAYS — drawn at the lock
        // until a 10m close takes it out (checked in the 10m block)
        // or the frame rolls. The case flipping or fading does not
        // remove it.
        bool shortLive = (fH > pH and fC < pH) or fC < pL
        if na(stopSP) and not stopSDead and shortLive and fH > pL
            stopSP := fH
        if not na(stopSP) and not stopSDead
            bool mergedH = false
            if array.size(grpPriceArr) > 0
                for k = 0 to array.size(grpPriceArr) - 1
                    if not mergedH and math.abs(stopSP - array.get(grpPriceArr, k)) / array.get(grpPriceArr, k) * 100 <= confPct
                        label.set_text(array.get(grpLabelArr, k), array.get(grpNamesArr, k) + " + STOP " + str.tostring(array.get(grpPriceArr, k), format.mintick) + array.get(grpConfArr, k))
                        mergedH := true
            if not mergedH
                array.push(_ln, line.new(tFormOpen, stopSP, tEnd, stopSP, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c_stop, width = widthStop, style = f_lstyle(styleStop)))
                array.push(_lb, label.new(tEnd, stopSP, "STOP " + str.tostring(stopSP, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_up, color = c_stop, textcolor = f_txtcol(c_stop), size = size.tiny))
        bool longLive = (fL < pL and fC > pL) or fC > pH
        if na(stopLP) and not stopLDead and longLive and fL < pH
            stopLP := fL
        if not na(stopLP) and not stopLDead
            bool mergedL = false
            if array.size(grpPriceArr) > 0
                for k = 0 to array.size(grpPriceArr) - 1
                    if not mergedL and math.abs(stopLP - array.get(grpPriceArr, k)) / array.get(grpPriceArr, k) * 100 <= confPct
                        label.set_text(array.get(grpLabelArr, k), array.get(grpNamesArr, k) + " + STOP " + str.tostring(array.get(grpPriceArr, k), format.mintick) + array.get(grpConfArr, k))
                        mergedL := true
            if not mergedL
                array.push(_ln, line.new(tFormOpen, stopLP, tEnd, stopLP, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c_stop, width = widthStop, style = f_lstyle(styleStop)))
                array.push(_lb, label.new(tEnd, stopLP, "STOP " + str.tostring(stopLP, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_down, color = c_stop, textcolor = f_txtcol(c_stop), size = size.tiny))
    // RANGE context lines — the mother candle's unbroken HIGH / LOW,
    // drawn from her open through the current candle. A side is
    // skipped when a frame line already sits on it (within confPct).
    if showRange and not na(rngHi) and not na(rngLo)
        int rT = na(rngT) ? tPriorOpen : rngT
        bool rHiDraw = true
        bool rLoDraw = true
        if array.size(grpPriceArr) > 0
            for k = 0 to array.size(grpPriceArr) - 1
                float gp = array.get(grpPriceArr, k)
                if math.abs(rngHi - gp) / gp * 100 <= confPct
                    rHiDraw := false
                if math.abs(rngLo - gp) / gp * 100 <= confPct
                    rLoDraw := false
        if rHiDraw
            array.push(_ln, line.new(rT, rngHi, tEnd, rngHi, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c_high, width = widthRange, style = f_lstyle(styleRange)))
            array.push(_lb, label.new(tEnd, rngHi, "RANGE HIGH " + str.tostring(rngHi, format.mintick) + f_conf(rngHi), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_up, color = c_high, textcolor = f_txtcol(c_high), size = size.tiny))
        if rLoDraw
            array.push(_ln, line.new(rT, rngLo, tEnd, rngLo, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c_low, width = widthRange, style = f_lstyle(styleRange)))
            array.push(_lb, label.new(tEnd, rngLo, "RANGE LOW " + str.tostring(rngLo, format.mintick) + f_conf(rngLo), xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_down, color = c_low, textcolor = f_txtcol(c_low), size = size.tiny))

// ── Lost → reclaim arrows (HIGH / LOW / CLOSE, 10m closes) ─────────
// Runs on every bar: each NEW completed 10m bar steps the three
// state machines once. State and arrows reset when the 4H frame
// rolls (a new prior candle = a new set of levels).
var label[] _arw = array.new_label()
var int frameKey = na
var float lastC10 = na
var float lastL10 = na
var float lastH10 = na
var int sideH = 0
var bool lostH = false
var int sideL = 0
var bool lostL = false
var int sideC = 0
var bool lostC = false
// RANGE (unbroken mother candle) crossing machines — SAME break/reclaim logic as the
// prior-4H high/low, judged on 10m closes. Reset when the range level itself changes
// (a new mother, or the range dies), tracked by its own key below — the range lives
// independently of the 4H frame.
var int sideRH = 0
var bool lostRH = false
var int sideRL = 0
var bool lostRL = false
var float lastRngHi = na
var float lastRngLo = na

if not na(tPriorOpen) and tPriorOpen != frameKey
    frameKey := tPriorOpen
    sideH := 0
    lostH := false
    sideL := 0
    lostL := false
    sideC := 0
    lostC := false
    stopSP := na
    stopSDead := false
    stopLP := na
    stopLDead := false
    lastC10 := na
    lastL10 := na
    lastH10 := na
    if array.size(_arw) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(_arw) - 1
            label.delete(array.get(_arw, i))
        array.clear(_arw)

// Each NEW completed 10m bar: check the locked stops (a 10m close
// beyond a stop takes it out — the line is removed for the rest of
// the candle) and step the lost → reclaim machines. A new completed
// bar is recognised by its close / low / high differing from the
// last sampled one — no fetched bar time is involved (see the
// fetch note above).
if not na(c10) and not na(pH) and not na(pL) and not na(pC) and (na(lastC10) or c10 != lastC10 or l10 != lastL10 or h10 != lastH10)
    lastC10 := c10
    lastL10 := l10
    lastH10 := h10
    if not na(stopSP) and not stopSDead and c10 > stopSP
        stopSDead := true
    if not na(stopLP) and not stopLDead and c10 < stopLP
        stopLDead := true
    // Step the crossing machines EVERY new 10m bar (needed for both arrows and
    // alerts — not gated by showRec, or the state would freeze when arrows are off).
    int ax = na(time[1]) ? time : time[1]
    [nsH, nlH, recH, flipH] = f_flip(sideH, lostH, c10, pH)
    sideH := nsH
    lostH := nlH
    [nsL, nlL, recL, flipL] = f_flip(sideL, lostL, c10, pL)
    sideL := nsL
    lostL := nlL
    [nsC, nlC, recC, flipC] = f_flip(sideC, lostC, c10, pC)
    sideC := nsC
    lostC := nlC
    // RANGE machines — reset when the range level changes (new mother / range died / first
    // appearance), then step the SAME break/reclaim machine on the range high & low. na
    // range = no step. NB: `value != na` is na (falsy) in Pine, so na transitions are
    // handled explicitly rather than with a bare `!=`.
    bool rhChanged = (na(rngHi) and not na(lastRngHi)) or (not na(rngHi) and (na(lastRngHi) or rngHi != lastRngHi))
    if rhChanged
        lastRngHi := rngHi
        sideRH := 0
        lostRH := false
    bool rlChanged = (na(rngLo) and not na(lastRngLo)) or (not na(rngLo) and (na(lastRngLo) or rngLo != lastRngLo))
    if rlChanged
        lastRngLo := rngLo
        sideRL := 0
        lostRL := false
    int nsRH = sideRH
    bool flipRH = false
    int nsRL = sideRL
    bool flipRL = false
    if not na(rngHi)
        [_nsrh, _nlrh, _recrh, _fliprh] = f_flip(sideRH, lostRH, c10, rngHi)
        sideRH := _nsrh
        lostRH := _nlrh
        nsRH := _nsrh
        flipRH := _fliprh
    if not na(rngLo)
        [_nsrl, _nlrl, _recrl, _fliprl] = f_flip(sideRL, lostRL, c10, rngLo)
        sideRL := _nsrl
        lostRL := _nlrl
        nsRL := _nsrl
        flipRL := _fliprl
    // Arrows (visual): HIGH / LOW / CLOSE crossings.
    if showRec
        if flipH and showHigh
            array.push(_arw, label.new(ax, nsH == 1 ? l10 : h10, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = nsH == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c_high, size = size.small))
        if flipL and showLow
            array.push(_arw, label.new(ax, nsL == 1 ? l10 : h10, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = nsL == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c_low, size = size.small))
        // CLOSE line is visual context only — no crossing arrow and no alert (signals
        // fire on HIGH / LOW / RANGE only). The close machine still steps above so the
        // CLOSE line can stay drawn, but it never marks or alerts.
        if flipRH and showRange
            array.push(_arw, label.new(ax, nsRH == 1 ? l10 : h10, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = nsRH == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c_high, size = size.small))
        if flipRL and showRange
            array.push(_arw, label.new(ax, nsRL == 1 ? l10 : h10, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = nsRL == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = c_low, size = size.small))
    // Signal alerts — prior-4H HIGH & LOW and the RANGE high & low, all through the SAME
    // break/reclaim machine and the SAME fourh_* types (OPEN / CLOSE stay drawing context).
    // Break = go-with (close through the level); reclaim / reject = fade (close back across).
    // Stop is the forming 4H candle's far extreme: HIGH for shorts, LOW for longs.
    if alertsOn
        // Prior-4H LOW
        if flipL
            if nsL == -1 and not na(fH)
                // closed below the prior 4H low → break down (go-with SHORT), stop = forming high
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_breakdn", "SHORT", c10, fH), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else if nsL == 1 and not na(fL)
                // reclaimed back above the prior 4H low → sweep-reclaim (fade LONG), stop = forming low
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_reclaim", "BUY", c10, fL), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        // Prior-4H HIGH
        if flipH
            if nsH == 1 and not na(fL)
                // closed above the prior 4H high → break up (go-with LONG), stop = forming low
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_breakup", "BUY", c10, fL), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else if nsH == -1 and not na(fH)
                // rejected back below the prior 4H high → failed break (fade SHORT), stop = forming high
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_reject", "SHORT", c10, fH), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        // RANGE LOW (same logic as the prior-4H low)
        if flipRL
            if nsRL == -1 and not na(fH)
                // closed below the range low → break down (go-with SHORT), stop = forming high
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_breakdn", "SHORT", c10, fH), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else if nsRL == 1 and not na(fL)
                // reclaimed back above the range low → sweep-reclaim (fade LONG), stop = forming low
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_reclaim", "BUY", c10, fL), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
        // RANGE HIGH (same logic as the prior-4H high)
        if flipRH
            if nsRH == 1 and not na(fL)
                // closed above the range high → break up (go-with LONG), stop = forming low
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_breakup", "BUY", c10, fL), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
            else if nsRH == -1 and not na(fH)
                // rejected back below the range high → failed break (fade SHORT), stop = forming high
                alert(f_sigJSON("fourh_reject", "SHORT", c10, fH), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
